IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tla-dates`
IMPORT `tla-rules`
IMPORT `tla-seat`

-- Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions (tla-seat.l4), the date helpers (tla-dates.l4)
-- and the time bar (tla-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from
-- the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are
-- illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`nd` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000
`adult born` MEANS `d` 1 1 1970

GIVEN `y` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`last day` `y` MEANS `the last day to commence is` `y`

§§ `Helpers: personal injury and death`

-- An adult with no spells and no fraud.
GIVEN `other Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `abuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `disc` IS A DATE, `extended` IS A BOOLEAN, `before 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`injury limit` `other Act` `abuse` `disc` `extended` `before 2018` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my injury or death action` `other Act` `abuse` `disc` `extended` `before 2018` `adult born` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd`

GIVEN `disc` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`plain injury limit` `disc` MEANS `injury limit` FALSE FALSE `disc` FALSE FALSE

-- With a minor's spell and an incapacity spell.
GIVEN `disc` IS A DATE, `born` IS A DATE, `minor` IS A BOOLEAN, `m from` IS A DATE, `m ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `m to` IS A DATE, `inc` IS A BOOLEAN, `i from` IS A DATE, `i ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `i to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`spell limit` `disc` `born` `minor` `m from` `m ended` `m to` `inc` `i from` `i ended` `i to` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my injury or death action` FALSE FALSE `disc` FALSE FALSE `born` `minor` `m from` `m ended` `m to` `inc` `i from` `i ended` `i to` FALSE FALSE `nd`

-- An adult with fraud or mistake.
GIVEN `disc` IS A DATE, `discovered` IS A BOOLEAN, `on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`fraud injury limit` `disc` `discovered` `on` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my injury or death action` FALSE FALSE `disc` FALSE FALSE `adult born` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` TRUE `discovered` `on`

GIVEN `other Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `abuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `disc` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`injury in time` `other Act` `abuse` `disc` `the day` MEANS
    `Can I still commence my injury or death action on this day` `other Act` `abuse` `disc` FALSE FALSE `adult born` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` `the day`

§§ `Helpers: other claims`

`contract` MEANS `a claim in contract or tort, other than for personal injury`
`statute sum` MEANS `a claim for a sum recoverable under an enactment, other than a penalty`
`deed` MEANS `a claim on a deed`
`judgment` MEANS `a claim on a judgment`
`interest` MEANS `a claim for arrears of interest`
`estate` MEANS `a claim to a deceased person's estate or a share in it`
`legacy interest` MEANS `a claim for arrears of interest on a legacy`
`trust fraud` MEANS `a beneficiary's claim against a trustee for fraud, or for trust property the trustee holds or converted`
`trust other` MEANS `a beneficiary's other claim for breach of trust or to recover trust property`
`ship` MEANS `a claim against a ship or its owners for damage, loss or injury caused by another ship's fault`
`tax` MEANS `a claim against the Crown or a public authority for money paid as a tax or under a mistake about a tax law`
`other kind` MEANS `another kind of claim`
`signed` MEANS `a written acknowledgement of my claim, signed by its maker`
`payment` MEANS `a payment in respect of my claim`
`unsigned` MEANS `an acknowledgement not in writing or not signed`
`none` MEANS `nothing of that kind`

-- An adult, nothing else.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `other Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `accrued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`flags limit` k `other Act` `accrued` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k `other Act` `accrued` `adult born` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `none` `nd` FALSE FALSE FALSE `nd`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `accrued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`adult limit` k `accrued` MEANS `flags limit` k FALSE `accrued`

-- Under 18, perhaps dead, perhaps a notice to proceed, perhaps through a predecessor.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `born` IS A DATE, `predecessor` IS A BOOLEAN, `died` IS A BOOLEAN, `died on` IS A DATE, `notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`minor limit` k `accrued` `born` `predecessor` `died` `died on` `notice` `notice on` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k FALSE `accrued` `born` FALSE FALSE `nd` `predecessor` `died` `died on` `notice` `notice on` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `none` `nd` FALSE FALSE FALSE `nd`

-- An adult incapable at accrual.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `ended on` IS A DATE, `notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`incapable limit` k `accrued` `ended` `ended on` `notice` `notice on` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k FALSE `accrued` `adult born` TRUE `ended` `ended on` FALSE FALSE `nd` `notice` `notice on` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `none` `nd` FALSE FALSE FALSE `nd`

-- An adult with fraud or mistake.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `discovered` IS A BOOLEAN, `on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`fraud limit` k `accrued` `discovered` `on` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k FALSE `accrued` `adult born` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` TRUE `discovered` `on` FALSE `none` `nd` FALSE FALSE FALSE `nd`

-- An adult with an acknowledgement or payment.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `debt` IS A BOOLEAN, `what` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement`, `on` IS A DATE, `by them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`ack limit` k `accrued` `debt` `what` `on` `by them` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k FALSE `accrued` `adult born` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` `debt` `what` `on` `by them` FALSE FALSE `nd`

-- Tax and ship claims, with the person under 18 at accrual (born 1 June 2010).
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN, `extended` IS A BOOLEAN, `to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`special limit` k `accrued` `overpayment` `extended` `to` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k FALSE `accrued` (`d` 1 6 2010) FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `none` `nd` FALSE `overpayment` `extended` `to`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`adult in time` k `accrued` `the day` MEANS
    `Can I still commence my action on this day` k FALSE `accrued` `adult born` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE FALSE `nd` FALSE `none` `nd` FALSE FALSE FALSE `nd` `the day`

§§ `Dates`

-- 3 years from 10 March 2020: anniversary 10 March 2023; from 29 February 2020: 28 February 2023 (fork F1). 3 years
-- commencing on 10 March 2020 end on 9 March 2023; commencing on 29 February 2020, on 28 February 2023 (fork F1);
-- commencing on 29 February 2020 for 4 years, on 28 February 2024 (2024 has a 29 February).
#ASSERT `the anniversary` 3 `years after` (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2023
#ASSERT `the anniversary` 3 `years after` (`d` 29 2 2020) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2023
#ASSERT `the last day of` 3 `years commencing on` (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `d` 9 3 2023
#ASSERT `the last day of` 3 `years commencing on` (`d` 29 2 2020) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2023
#ASSERT `the last day of` 4 `years commencing on` (`d` 29 2 2020) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2024
#ASSERT `the last day of` 3 `years commencing on` (`d` 1 1 2020) EQUALS `d` 31 12 2022

§§ `s 2(2), (3) -- disability`

#ASSERT `Am I under disability` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I under disability` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I under disability` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I under disability` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I under disability` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 26A(4) -- relevant person`

-- A minor not in a parent's custody; in the custody of a capable parent; of a parent who is under disability, is the
-- person to be sued, or could be influenced.
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An adult incapable for 28 days or more: no representative; an independent one; one who could be influenced; and an
-- adult incapable for less than 28 days with no representative.
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5A(6) -- personal representative`

-- The deceased knew on 1 March 2020; appointed 1 June 2021, knew before: the earliest is 1 March 2020.
#ASSERT `What is my date of discoverability as personal representative` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 1 6 2021) (`d` 1 1 2021) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2020
-- The deceased did not know; the representative knew before appointment: (b), the appointment day.
#ASSERT `What is my date of discoverability as personal representative` FALSE `nd` (`d` 1 6 2021) (`d` 1 1 2021) EQUALS `d` 1 6 2021
-- The representative learnt after appointment: (c), that day.
#ASSERT `What is my date of discoverability as personal representative` FALSE `nd` (`d` 1 6 2021) (`d` 1 9 2021) EQUALS `d` 1 9 2021
-- Learnt on the appointment day itself.
#ASSERT `What is my date of discoverability as personal representative` FALSE `nd` (`d` 1 6 2021) (`d` 1 6 2021) EQUALS `d` 1 6 2021

§§ `s 5A(5), s 38A(3) -- extension to 6 years`

-- Accrued before 1 July 2018: discoverability on 30 June 2015 is more than 3 years before (no); on 1 July 2015, exactly 3
-- years (yes). Accrued after: yes.
#ASSERT `Can a judge extend my time to 6 years` TRUE (`d` 30 6 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can a judge extend my time to 6 years` TRUE (`d` 1 7 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a judge extend my time to 6 years` FALSE (`d` 1 8 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `Personal injury and death: the time limit`

-- s 5A(3): 3 years commencing on the date of discoverability.
#ASSERT `plain injury limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 9 3 2023)
#ASSERT `plain injury limit` (`d` 29 2 2020) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 28 2 2023)
-- s 5A(5): extended to 6 years; s 38A(3) stops it for an old claim discovered before 1 July 2015; allows it from that day.
#ASSERT `injury limit` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `last day` (`d` 9 3 2026)
#ASSERT `injury limit` FALSE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2015) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `last day` (`d` 29 6 2018)
#ASSERT `injury limit` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 7 2015) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `last day` (`d` 30 6 2021)
-- s 38: another Act; s 5B: child abuse.
#ASSERT `injury limit` TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `another Act's time limit applies`
#ASSERT `injury limit` FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 3 1985) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no limitation period applies`
-- s 32: not yet discovered; discovered 1 January 2022, so 3 years commencing then end 31 December 2024; discovered
-- before the date of discoverability, which governs.
#ASSERT `fraud injury limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `time has not yet begun to count`
#ASSERT `fraud injury limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2022) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 31 12 2024)
#ASSERT `fraud injury limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2019) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 9 3 2023)

§§ `Personal injury: s 26A suspension`

-- Born 1 June 2010, discoverability 1 June 2020, a minor without a capable parent from then: the spell runs to 31 May
-- 2028, the day before the 18th birthday; 2,922 days (8 years with 29 February 2024 and 2028) are added to 31 May 2023:
-- 31 May 2031.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 6 2020) (`d` 1 6 2010) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` EQUALS `last day` (`d` 31 5 2031)
-- The same spell ended on 30 November 2020: 183 days added to 31 May 2023: 30 November 2023.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 6 2020) (`d` 1 6 2010) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE (`d` 30 11 2020) FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` EQUALS `last day` (`d` 30 11 2023)
-- A spell that began before the date of discoverability counts only from it: 1 January 2020 to 30 November 2020 still
-- adds 183 days.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 6 2020) (`d` 1 6 2010) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 30 11 2020) FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` EQUALS `last day` (`d` 30 11 2023)
-- An adult (discoverability 10 March 2020) incapable 1 to 27 January 2021: 27 days, under 28, no effect; 1 to 28
-- January: 28 days added to 9 March 2023: 6 April 2023.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) `adult born` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2021) TRUE (`d` 27 1 2021) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 9 3 2023)
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) `adult born` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2021) TRUE (`d` 28 1 2021) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 6 4 2023)
-- Incapacity that has not ended: no last day yet.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) `adult born` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2021) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `no last day yet, because the disability or suspension has not ended`
-- Incapacity beginning the day after the last day (10 March 2023), not ended: no effect.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) `adult born` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` TRUE (`d` 10 3 2023) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `last day` (`d` 9 3 2023)
-- Incapacity beginning on the last day, 9 March to 9 April 2023 (32 days): 10 April 2023.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 10 3 2020) `adult born` FALSE `nd` FALSE `nd` TRUE (`d` 9 3 2023) TRUE (`d` 9 4 2023) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 10 4 2023)
-- Two overlapping spells (born 1 January 2005, discoverability 1 January 2020): minor 1 January 2020 to 31 December
-- 2021 (731 days), incapacity 1 January 2021 to 30 June 2022 (181 days beyond the first): 31 December 2022 + 912 days =
-- 30 June 2025.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2005) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2021) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2021) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2022) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 30 6 2025)
-- Incapacity first (1 January to 30 June 2020), minor spell inside and beyond it (1 March to 31 December 2020): together
-- 366 days of 2020, added to 31 December 2022: 1 January 2024 (days counted, fork F4).
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2005) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2020) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 1 1 2024)
-- A spell wholly inside another adds nothing more: minor 1 January to 31 December 2020, incapacity 1 March to 30 June
-- 2020: 1 January 2024.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2005) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2020) EQUALS `last day` (`d` 1 1 2024)

§§ `Personal injury: commencing on a day`

-- Last day 9 March 2023: commencing that day is in time, the next day is not; before the date of discoverability is in
-- time; another Act: not answered; child abuse: any day.
#ASSERT `injury in time` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) (`d` 9 3 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `injury in time` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) (`d` 10 3 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `injury in time` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) (`d` 1 1 2019) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `injury in time` TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) (`d` 1 1 2021) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `injury in time` FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 3 1985) (`d` 1 1 2060) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 5B -- child abuse`

#ASSERT `Can I bring my child abuse action at any time` TRUE `sexual abuse` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I bring my child abuse action at any time` TRUE `serious physical abuse` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I bring my child abuse action at any time` TRUE `psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I bring my child abuse action at any time` TRUE `other abuse or harm` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I bring my child abuse action at any time` TRUE `sexual abuse` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I bring my child abuse action at any time` TRUE `sexual abuse` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I bring my child abuse action at any time` FALSE `sexual abuse` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 5C -- settled child abuse claims`

-- Settled 30 June 2018, the day before s 5B commenced, after a period had expired: may apply; once set aside, may sue.
#ASSERT `What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` `sexual abuse` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2018) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you may apply to the court to set the settlement aside, and may sue once it does`
#ASSERT `What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` `serious physical abuse` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2018) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the settlement has been set aside: you may bring the action`
-- Settled on 1 July 2018; before a period expired; a lawful act; other harm; an adult: not reopened.
#ASSERT `What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` `sexual abuse` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 7 2018) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this is not a previously settled child abuse claim that section 5C reopens`
#ASSERT `What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` `sexual abuse` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2018) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this is not a previously settled child abuse claim that section 5C reopens`
#ASSERT `What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` `serious physical abuse` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this is not a previously settled child abuse claim that section 5C reopens`
#ASSERT `What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` `other abuse or harm` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this is not a previously settled child abuse claim that section 5C reopens`
#ASSERT `What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` `sexual abuse` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this is not a previously settled child abuse claim that section 5C reopens`
-- An accepted National Redress Scheme offer (s 5C(8)), even with the other facts met.
#ASSERT `What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` `sexual abuse` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `section 5C does not apply to an accepted National Redress Scheme offer`
-- s 5C(6), (7).
#ASSERT `How much of my earlier settlement can the court take into account` 100000 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 100000
#ASSERT `How much of my earlier settlement can the court take into account` 100000 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 50000
#ASSERT `How much of my earlier settlement can the court take into account` 75001 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 37500.5
#ASSERT `How much of my earlier settlement can the court take into account` 100000 FALSE TRUE 30000 EQUALS JUST 30000
-- s 5C(5).
#ASSERT `Can the other party get back what it paid me` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the other party get back what it paid me` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

